BBRv3 4.14 port checks
=====================

Run from the repository root:

  python3 tools/testing/selftests/bbr3/test_backport.py --self-test-negatives
  python3 tools/testing/selftests/bbr3/test_backport.py \
      --cc /path/to/exact/aosp/clang --sanitize --self-test-negatives
  python3 tools/testing/selftests/bbr3/test_provenance.py
  python3 tools/testing/selftests/bbrplus/test_backport.py

The model runner extracts the actual BBRv3 algorithm, TCP rate code, metadata,
loss notification, split/merge blocks, TLP classification and BPF member policy.
It substitutes host socket/clock/queue/BTF fixtures. It is NOT an emulated TCP
stack, boot test, network stress test, or performance benchmark. The source
fragment extraction and host ABI checks complement, not replace, AArch64 target
compilation and a complete kernel link.

Coverage: 10,000 wrap cases; 74,100 split/merge cases; 1,188 TSO dispatch cases; CE/loss counter wrap;
legacy bytes vs packet-valued snapshots on CC switches; missing/reneged rate
samples; newly counted/retransmitted loss; immediate loss-bound reaction;
STARTUP, DRAIN, all four PROBE_BW phases, PROBE_RTT entry/exit; TLP advancing,
ambiguous, DSACK, pure-dupack and new-data ACKs; 20/52-byte diagnostic ABI;
NULL/unsupported native callbacks in BPF struct_ops. Thirteen mutations must
compile but fail a runtime assertion. A compiler failure is not a passing
negative control. --mutant is for intentional individual failures only.

The additive zero-context source patch and manifest preserve the historical
BPF source seals. test_provenance.py verifies current endpoints, all three BPF
before-image chains, protected BBR/BBRplus/TCP-buffer sources, and actual
reverse/forward replay. They are reproducibility/integrity records, not signed
supply-chain attestation or device proof. Refresh them deliberately only after
reviewing a later edit; a hash mismatch is not permission to accept drift.

See Documentation/networking/bbr3-backport.rst for port exclusions, selection
and a sender-side phone comparison procedure. The default remains bbrplus.
